From: Audio speakers <audio-speakers@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH candidate] ASoC: qcom: consume the VI calibration events

The Windows ACDB driver parses two DSP custom events (REA 2026-11-05,
qcadcm8380.sys FUN_140083d00):

  EVENT_ID_VI_CALIBRATION (0x0800119f)
      [num_ch][state][R0_ch0]...[R0_chN], state 4 = success, 5 = failure
      (ParseAndSendSpeakerProtectionCalibPayload)
  EVENT_ID_VI_PER_SPKR_CALIBRATION (0x08001511)
      [num_ch][state_0][R0_0][state_1][R0_1]..., per-channel state
      (ParseAndSendSpeakerProtectionPerSpkrCalibPayload)

Register both next to the SP diagnostics event, route them from q6apm and
accept a successful event as a measured (non-nominal) calibration through the
guard's existing generation path. Graph identity, caps, the CPS policy and the
fault latch still gate unmute, and an invalid or malformed event changes
nothing, so the guard stays fail-closed without a valid measurement.

R0 is Q24, matching the registry R0CalQ24 value Windows reads.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
